WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:05.478
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:23.310
BILL KIRBY: So welcome to Kunshan Duke Daxue, Duke Kunshan University.

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:30.190
And here we are at DKU in its final months of construction

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:33.650
in the middle of Kunshan in the middle of Jiangsu provence.

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:36.360
And I'm here with Dr. Mary Brown Bullock,

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:39.610
who's the executive vice chancellor for Duke Kunshan University.

00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:41.835
And Mary thank you very much for welcoming us.

00:00:41.835 --> 00:00:43.960
MARY BROWN BULLOCK: Well, thank you for being here.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:45.597
This is you fourth, fifth, sixth time?

00:00:45.597 --> 00:00:47.180
BILL KIRBY: I've been here many times.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:48.120
MARY BROWN BULLOCK: Many times, right.

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:50.120
So you've seen these building grown.

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:51.911
BILL KIRBY: I've seen these buildings grow.

00:00:51.911 --> 00:00:55.400
And I've seen grow here-- and I've never imagined quite frankly it

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:59.380
would be as beautiful as it is, this main academic building.

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:03.260
But we're in the middle of the most ambitious American effort

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:05.800
in higher education in China, since the building

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:09.860
of the Yenching University in the late 1920s, a university that

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:14.880
would have an enormous impact on China in the Republican period and then

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:18.270
still today as the campus of Peking University.

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:23.381
So Mary tell us what's behind us and what's going on.

00:01:23.381 --> 00:01:25.130
MARY BROWN BULLOCK: Well, as Bill said, we

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:29.080
are in the final months of construction Duke Kunshan University.

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:32.440
We will open in August for our first classes.

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:35.070
BILL KIRBY: Of 2014, so this may be aired after that.

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:37.990
MARY BROWN BULLOCK: 2014, and the building behind you

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:40.170
is the centerpiece of the campus.

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:43.000
We call it the academic building.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.843
You can see that it has-- I don't know if you can pick up

00:01:45.843 --> 00:01:51.100
the fine glass edging, but it has some elements from Suzhou Gardens,

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:54.380
as well as having a very distinct, modern look.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:58.270
And I think that's what this campus is designed to do.

00:01:58.270 --> 00:02:01.220
It'll be a cutting edge technologically.

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:06.360
But aesthetically it tries to draw on the region we're in, the Jiangnan

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:10.699
region, particularly the Suzhou region with canals and lakes.

00:02:10.699 --> 00:02:15.420
You can't see it here, but there will be water everywhere on campus.

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:18.170
And instead of a grass quadrangle, we have

00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:20.730
a lake in the center of the campus.

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:22.750
So this is one of the ways that we're trying

00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:25.990
to really develop the elements of the region.

00:02:25.990 --> 00:02:31.320
This building will house faculty, students, auditorium, classrooms,

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:32.640
dining room.

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:34.960
It's about 200,000 square feet.

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:39.230
But as you can also see, we have four additional buildings,

00:02:39.230 --> 00:02:41.310
which will be opening this fall.

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:45.720
And we will have housing for 200 students, a 200 bed conference center.

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:47.942
You're welcome to come and use our conference center.

00:02:47.942 --> 00:02:49.160
BILL KIRBY: Thank you.

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:51.220
MARY BROWN BULLOCK: And a service building.

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:55.140
So this is really the beginning of Duke Kunshan University.

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:57.580
BILL KIRBY: And it's phase one of Duke Kunshan University.

00:02:57.580 --> 00:03:02.840
It's phase one of three on a 200 acre campus right

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:07.990
in the heart of the fastest developing part of China between Shanghai

00:03:07.990 --> 00:03:12.680
and Nanjing-- right in the heart of what may someday be, I think,

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:15.260
a city called Nanhai-- Nanjing-Shanghai.

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:18.960
Or maybe not just a city, because this will ideally remain green.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:22.720
Now in terms of getting around, so much water here, will you have gondolas?

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:25.470
MARY BROWN BULLOCK: No, I don't think-- we have beautiful bridges.

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:30.010
We have beautiful bridges that evoke a Chinese bridge feeling.

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:33.860
But it's actually true that when you come from the student dormitory

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:36.155
to the classroom, you have to go across two bridges.

00:03:36.155 --> 00:03:38.870
So that will be kind of fun.

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:43.410
I think we all enjoy seeing the lake in its final manifestations.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:45.760
BILL KIRBY: Well, we're here right before the opening.

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:48.630
And this will air after the opening.

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:52.040
And we'll know a bit more at that point how things have gone.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:56.150
But it's an extraordinary effort and extraordinary ambition

00:03:56.150 --> 00:03:58.560
on the part of Duke and also on the part of Kunshan.

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:00.227
So congratulations, you're almost there.

00:04:00.227 --> 00:04:01.851
MARY BROWN BULLOCK: We're almost there.

00:04:01.851 --> 00:04:03.180
BILL KIRBY: Thanks, Mary

